                <pb facs="0312" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-13T15:00:00-05:00">December 13, 1948—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1812. Urtel 2501 Dec 11. In conversations with Madame Chiang both President and
                    Secretary have expressed sympathy with Chinese difficulties but have not given
                    any indication of any change in US position and have made no commitments beyond
                    implementation present China Aid Program.</p>
                <p>For your info neither Amb Koo nor any other Chi official was present during
                    Madame’s conversation with President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
